      "side": 1,
      "message": "FYI, the way this works is that the `open-dice` library gets built with this symbol unresolved, the assumption being that the final link stage would provide it. IMO, this kind of setup only makes sense if the `open-dice` client (e.g. `pvmfw`) implements the function. However, this CL proposes moving the symbol into yet another component (`libvmbase`), which doesn\u0027t even use `open-dice`.\n\nAt this point, I think that it might make more sense to have a small library that only provides the symbol, for a particular configuration (say `lib_open_dice_clear_memory_baremetal` or so) and explicitly link against it when linking the final client (`pvmfw`). That way, we also clean up the somewhat cyclic dependency (\"client needs library but library needs symbol from client\").",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 114,
        "startChar": 21,
        "endLine": 114,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "e69d32a1d283bffd3d539d06ad11931c809bbe36",
